[%operation Z!ParamAction parseParamAction(): String{
	
	return  "(" + self.circusAction.parseAction() + ")";
}%]

[%operation Z!ParallelAction parseParallelAction(): String{
	return  "(" + self.leftAction.parseAction() + "\r\n" + "		\\<lbrakk> " + self.channelSet.parseChannelSet() + " \\<rbrakk> " + "\r\n" + "		" + self.rightAction.parseAction() + ")";
}%]


[%operation Z!ParallelActionIte parseParallelActionIte(): String{
	return  "(" + " \\<lbrakk> " + self.channelSet.parseChannelSet() + " \\<rbrakk> " + self.declList.decls.at(0).parseVarDeclInIteAct() + " \\<bullet> " + self.circusAction.parseAction() + ")";
}%]
[*suppose there is only one parameter for iteration*]


[%operation Z!InterleaveActionIte parseInterleaveActionIte(): String{
	return  "( \\<interleave> "  +  self.declList.decls.at(0).parseVarDeclInIteAct() + " \\<bullet>  " + self.circusAction.parseAction() + " )";
}%]
[*suppose there is only one parameter for iteration*]

[%operation Z!InterleaveAction parseInterleaveAction(): String{
	return  "(" + self.leftAction.parseAction() + " \\<interleave> " +	self.rightAction.parseAction() + ")";
}%]


[%operation Z!RenameAction parseRenameAction(): String{
	if(self.assignmentPairs.size()>0){
	return  "(" + self.circusAction.parseAction() + " \\<lbrakk> " + self.assignmentPairs.parseAssignmentPairs() + " \\<rbrakk> \\<lbrakk>\\<rbrakk>)";}
	else {
	return  "(" + self.circusProcess.parseProc();
	}
}%]

[%operation Z!VarDecl parseVarDeclInIteAct(): String{
	//assume there is only one parameter for iteration
	var var_name = self.nameList.names.at(0).word;
	var var_range = self.expr.parseExpr();
	
	return  var_name + " \\<in> " + var_range;
}%]


[%operation Z!ZName parse(): String{
	//renaming left-hand sides can be event values too, e.g. c__in\<^bold>.x (see holEvent)
	return  self.word.holEvent();
}%]

[*RC2Z.eol writes event values with the CyPhyCircus channel-instantiation syntax c\<^bold>.v (needed by circusM2T.egl).
  In HOL-CSP an event value is a datatype constructor application, so inside renamings and channel sets it must be
  written (c v): \<^bold>. is only valid in a prefix c\<^bold>.v \<rightarrow> P, and \<cdot> is HOLCF continuous-function application,
  which does not type-check for chan_event constructors ("Clash of types _ => _ and _ -> _").
  Prefixes are unaffected: there the \<^bold>. comes from parseField, not from a name; (c v) \<rightarrow> P would also be valid.

  Design background:
  - RC2Z.eol produces ONE Z model that is shared by circusM2T.egl (IsaCircus/CyPhyCircus), circusM2T_HOLCSP.egl and
    circusM2T_HOLCSP_trans_core.egl. Event values in renamings and channel sets are stored there as plain name strings
    (e.g. RefExpr "internal__X\<^bold>.NID_Y"), not as structured expressions.
  - circusM2T.egl prints that string unchanged (\<^bold>. is the IsaCircus syntax, confirmed by Simon); the HOL-CSP
    templates translate it here, at the two places where names are printed (ZName.parse and the RefExpr case of parseExpr).
  - It cannot simply be done in RC2Z.eol: whichever syntax the EOL writes into the shared string, one of the targets is wrong.
  Dependency / risk: this relies on RC2Z.eol writing exactly "\<^bold>." (tevent_str and renameTriggerEventsPairL).
    If that marker is changed in the EOL (e.g. back to \<cdot>), this translation silently stops working and the
    HOL-CSP output is wrong without any error. Change both together.
  Long-term: store event values in the Z model as structured applications (ApplExpr: channel applied to argument),
    printed by each template in its own syntax; then holEvent can be removed. This also helps project_triggers
    (binding the event arguments). Note that renaming left-hand sides (AssignmentPairs.lhsElement) are a ZNameList,
    i.e. names only, so they need a different representation.*]
[%operation String holEvent(): String{
	var marker = "\\<^bold>.";
	if(self.indexOf(marker) < 0){
		return self;
	}
	var result = "";
	var rest = self;
	var i = rest.indexOf(marker);
	while(i >= 0){
		result = result + rest.substring(0, i) + " ";
		rest = rest.substring(i + marker.length());
		i = rest.indexOf(marker);
	}
	return "(" + result + rest + ")";
}%]




